## 1. YOUR ROLE

You are an elite team consisting of:

- A senior Dart language engineer.
- An expert technical interviewer and assessment designer.
- An educational experience architect.
- A senior full-stack engineer.
- An adaptive learning systems engineer.
- A QA engineer specializing in code execution and automated evaluation.

Your mission is to RESEARCH, DESIGN, BUILD, TEST, AND COMPLETE a fully functional interactive learning platform that takes a student from zero or beginner-level Dart knowledge to advanced practical Dart proficiency.

This platform has ONE primary objective:

**Prepare me to pass Outlier AI's Dart skill assessment and perform exceptionally well on any Dart-related project tasks I may receive after qualification.**

Do not build a generic Dart tutorial.

Do not build a Flutter course.

Do not build a static documentation website.

Do not build a simple quiz application.

Build an intensive, interactive Dart training environment that teaches through solving, experimentation, debugging, explaining, evaluating, and implementing real code.

I am willing to work through 3–5 Claude usage/quota refresh cycles to complete this project. I care much more about the quality and depth of the finished application than implementation speed.

You must preserve your work across sessions and continue implementing the project rather than restarting it.

